        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "K. Leave for Family Bereavement—A unit member shall be allowed a maximum of five (5) days of absence without loss of salary upon the death of a child, parent (natural, foster, or in-law), brother, sister, husband, wife, or of anyone who lives regularly in his/her household. A unit member shall be allowed a maximum of two (2) duty days of absence without loss of salary upon the death of a brother-in-law, sister-in-law, son-in-law, daughter-in-law, grandparent, grandchild, or spouse's grandparent. In the event of unusual travel or personal problems in connection with the use of bereavement leave, additional leave days may be granted by the appropriate official.",
